nux commands are modular. You change how a command behaves by adding flags (also called arguments, switches, or options):

Short options: Start with a single dash (-) and a single letter:

ls -a (displays all files)

ls -l (displays detailed file metadata: permissions, size, date)

Combine them together: ls -la (lists all files in long detailed format)

Long options: Start with two dashes (--) and use full words:

ls --all (identical to ls -a)

ls --help
